  "notes": "Coins for the small price; wind for the twisting of the Book (no tongues drawn). Nothing on the negated favours of 77:10-24 or the punishment. STAGING v4: 77: As-Sa'di: anyone who takes something of this world for a right of Allah or of people, and whoever swears an oath to take property: in a market at dusk one man (s) swears (speak, 77:6) and receives a small price (77:7, coins plate); the Hereafter (77:10-27) is not pictured, he simply stays in view. 78: 78:2-3: only part of the People of the Book (f) twists the Book: they read (78:4) and speak (78:6, 78:14, 78:24) before listeners (l); the rest (o) stay still. Wind plate for the twisting, ending before the Names."
